.page unzip 1 list, test and extract zip archives

# SYNOPSIS
*unzip* [*-ltpoqn*] [*-d* _DIR_] _ARCHIVE_[.zip] [_MEMBER_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`unzip` extracts the members of a zip archive. Stored and deflated members are supported; each member is checked against its recorded CRC-32 and size while it is unpacked, and a damaged or truncated archive is reported rather than half-extracted. _MEMBER_ operands are glob patterns that select members (quote them so the shell leaves them alone).

Members with *..* in their name or with an absolute path are not extracted, and a member is never written through a symbolic link. Unix permissions, symbolic links and modification times stored in the archive are restored. Existing files are not overwritten unless *-o* is given.

Not supported: zip64, encrypted members, other compression methods and multi-disk archives (each is reported by name).

# OPTIONS
@ *-l*
    List the members with their sizes and times.
@ *-t*
    Test: unpack every member without writing it anywhere, and check its CRC-32 and size.
@ *-p*
    Write the contents of the members to standard output.
@ *-o*
    Overwrite existing files.
@ *-n*
    Never overwrite, and do not complain about it.
@ *-q*
    Quiet.
@ *-d* _DIR_
    Extract below _DIR_, creating it if needed.

# EXIT STATUS
0, 1 if a member could not be extracted or failed its check, 2 if the archive cannot be read at all.

# EXAMPLES
    unzip -l photos.zip
    unzip -d /tmp/photos photos.zip
    unzip -p notes.zip a.txt | head

# SEE ALSO
zip(1), tar(1), gzip(1)
